      "body": "## Purpose\n\nFixes #55725. GLM-5.3-Flash crashes at weight load on multi-node (2×8 H100) with `KeyError: 'layers.11.self_attn.fused_qkv_a_proj.weight'` on every second-node worker, while single-node runs fine.\n\n## Root cause\n\nWith 2 nodes the run is pipeline-parallel (PP=2), so layer 11's params exist only on stage-0 ranks. The attached log (`layer11.log`) shows all `Worker_PP1_TP0..7` crashing; PP0 is clean. The normal load path guards every weight with `is_pp_missing_parameter` (glm5next/common/model.py), but the two FP8-dequant fast paths bypass it and index `params_dict` directly:\n\n- `_try_load_fp8_attn_proj` → `params_dict[target_w]` (the traceback in the issue)\n- `_try_load_fp8_indexer_wk` → `params_dict[fused_name]` (same class of hole)\n\nOn a PP rank that doesn't hold the layer, `params_dict` has no such key → KeyError before the normal path ever gets a chance to skip the weight.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn both fast paths, return `False` when the target param is absent from `params_dict`, so the weight falls through to the normal path, which skips it via `is_pp_missing_parameter`. The indexer-wk guard is placed *before* buffering, so PP ranks also don't accumulate fp8 tensors that nobody loads. Behavior on ranks that hold the layer is byte-identical.\n\n## Verification\n\nNo multi-node GPU here, so verified by driving both functions directly with the exact crashing weight names, on the MI350X pod against the patched module:\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| PP1-style params_dict (layer 11 absent), fp8 `q_a_proj` weight + scale | not consumed, nothing loaded → falls to normal skip path (was: KeyError) |\n| PP0-style control (BF16 `fused_qkv_a_proj` present) | consumed + loaded, unchanged |\n| PP1, indexer `wk` weight + scale | not consumed → normal skip |\n| PP0 control, indexer `wk` | consumed + loaded, unchanged |\n\nPre-commit: all hooks pass. Single-node (TP-only) behavior is untouched — the guards only trigger when the target param is missing.\n",
      "changedFiles": 1,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "mustafayildirim"
            },
            "body": "Ping for review — fixes the #55725 multi-node weight-load crash. Root-caused from the attached log: every `Worker_PP1` rank dies with `KeyError` because the two FP8-dequant fast paths index `params_dict` without the `is_pp_missing_parameter` guard the normal path has. Verified on MI350X with the exact crashing weight names (PP1-style params_dict falls through to the skip path; PP0 ranks load byte-identically).\n\n@gdhyi @dllehr-amd\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-18T23:45:44Z",
            "databaseId": 5737527680,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-18T23:45:44Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-5737527680"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "fasuizu-br"
            },
            "body": "Same KeyError on a single node: `--tensor-parallel-size 4 --pipeline-parallel-size 2` on 8× H100 (image `vllm/vllm-openai:glm53-flash-cu129` as pulled on 2026-08-26, sha256:3b9ab05f…) fails in the PP1 workers with `KeyError: 'layers.11.self_attn.fused_qkv_a_proj.weight'`, while TP8 on the same node loads fine. So PP=2 on one node is enough to verify the fix; no multi-node setup is needed. The code comments say PP is gated off, but `Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration` inherits `SupportsPP` from `Glm4vForConditionalGeneration`, so `--pipeline-parallel-size 2` passes the config check and the failure only shows up in the loader (`_try_load_fp8_attn_proj` in `vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py`).\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-25T15:35:56Z",
            "databaseId": 5835077681,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-25T15:35:56Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-5835077681"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "mustafayildirim"
            },
            "body": "Thanks — that's a much easier repro, and it confirms the diagnosis: the failure is the loader, not anything multi-node-specific. / index `params_dict` directly for layer names that only exist on the PP stage that owns layer 11, so any PP>1 rank without the layer hits the KeyError. (The fix in this PR guards both lookups and lets those weights fall through to the normal `is_pp_missing_parameter` skip path — verified on MI350X with the exact crashing weight names.) If you pull the branch, the single-node TP4/PP2 repro should load clean; if you'd rather not build, I can post the patched module for your image.",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-09T22:48:46Z",
            "databaseId": 6090578860,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-09T22:48:46Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-6090578860"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "mustafayildirim"
            },
            "body": "Sorry — markdown escaping glitch in my last comment: the two functions are `_try_load_fp8_attn_proj` and `_try_load_fp8_indexer_wk`, and they index `params_dict` directly for layer names that only exist on the PP stage owning that layer. Any PP>1 rank without the layer hits the KeyError before the normal `is_pp_missing_parameter` skip path is reached.\n\nYour single-node TP4/PP2 repro on 8×H100 should load clean with this branch — the guards make both fast paths decline for PP-missing layers and fall through to the standard skip.\n",
