  "inline_comments": [],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Ping for review — fixes the #55725 multi-node weight-load crash. Root-caused from the attached log: every `Worker_PP1` rank dies with `KeyError` because the two FP8-dequant fast paths index `params_dict` without the `is_pp_missing_parameter` guard the normal path has. Verified on MI350X with the exact crashing weight names (PP1-style params_dict falls through to the skip path; PP0 ranks load byte-identically).\n\n@gdhyi @dllehr-amd\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-18T23:45:44Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-5737527680",
      "id": 5737527680,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-18T23:45:44Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mustafayildirim"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Same KeyError on a single node: `--tensor-parallel-size 4 --pipeline-parallel-size 2` on 8× H100 (image `vllm/vllm-openai:glm53-flash-cu129` as pulled on 2026-08-26, sha256:3b9ab05f…) fails in the PP1 workers with `KeyError: 'layers.11.self_attn.fused_qkv_a_proj.weight'`, while TP8 on the same node loads fine. So PP=2 on one node is enough to verify the fix; no multi-node setup is needed. The code comments say PP is gated off, but `Glm5NextForConditionalGeneration` inherits `SupportsPP` from `Glm4vForConditionalGeneration`, so `--pipeline-parallel-size 2` passes the config check and the failure only shows up in the loader (`_try_load_fp8_attn_proj` in `vllm/models/glm5next/common/model.py`).\n",
      "created_at": "2026-09-25T15:35:56Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-5835077681",
      "id": 5835077681,
      "updated_at": "2026-09-25T15:35:56Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "fasuizu-br"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Thanks — that's a much easier repro, and it confirms the diagnosis: the failure is the loader, not anything multi-node-specific. / index `params_dict` directly for layer names that only exist on the PP stage that owns layer 11, so any PP>1 rank without the layer hits the KeyError. (The fix in this PR guards both lookups and lets those weights fall through to the normal `is_pp_missing_parameter` skip path — verified on MI350X with the exact crashing weight names.) If you pull the branch, the single-node TP4/PP2 repro should load clean; if you'd rather not build, I can post the patched module for your image.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T22:48:46Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-6090578860",
      "id": 6090578860,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T22:48:46Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mustafayildirim"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Sorry — markdown escaping glitch in my last comment: the two functions are `_try_load_fp8_attn_proj` and `_try_load_fp8_indexer_wk`, and they index `params_dict` directly for layer names that only exist on the PP stage owning that layer. Any PP>1 rank without the layer hits the KeyError before the normal `is_pp_missing_parameter` skip path is reached.\n\nYour single-node TP4/PP2 repro on 8×H100 should load clean with this branch — the guards make both fast paths decline for PP-missing layers and fall through to the standard skip.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T22:49:24Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/57639#issuecomment-6090585612",
      "id": 6090585612,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-09T22:49:24Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "mustafayildirim"
      }
    }
  ],
